From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: release direct vports with node

A WLAN recovery destroys and recreates its direct-switch node before
mac80211 reconstructs the virtual interfaces.  Direct virtual-port
references previously survived that destruction in the PPE-wide VP table,
so every recovery leaked a reference and left peer routing associated with
a node instance that no longer existed.

Add a node-wide detach helper and use the normal detach path for every
reference.  This preserves shared MLO ports owned by other running nodes,
invalidates the removed node's flow profiles and releases the slot when its
last user disappears.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.c
@@ -712,6 +712,19 @@ bool ppe_vp_ds_detach(struct ppe_device
 	return true;
 }
 
+void ppe_vp_ds_node_detach(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int node)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	if (node < 0 || node >= PPE_VP_DS_NODES)
+		return;
+
+	/* A node may own several link-vif references to one shared MLO VP. */
+	for (i = 0; i < PPE_VP_SLOTS; i++)
+		while (ppe_vp_ds_detach(ppe_dev, PPE_VP_PORT_BASE + i, node))
+			;
+}
+
 int ppe_vp_ds_peer_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int port, int node,
 		       const u8 *addr, bool enable)
 {
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_vp.h
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ int ppe_vp_ds_attach(struct ppe_device *
 		     int queue, int node);
 bool ppe_vp_ds_detach(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int vp, int node);
 void ppe_vp_ds_node_state(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int node, bool up);
+void ppe_vp_ds_node_detach(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int node);
 int ppe_vp_ds_peer_set(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int vp, int node,
 		       const u8 *addr, bool enable);
 int ppe_vp_ds_node_get(struct ppe_device *ppe_dev, int vp, const u8 *addr);
